# Core conventions

Follow `docs/ENGINEERING.md`. Summary for every change:

## Non-negotiables

- Async-first request path (aiosqlite / Motor). No new sync I/O in handlers (bcrypt is the known exception).
- No ORM. Parameterized SQL in helpers; schema in `app/db/schema.sql`.
- Pydantic = request/response only, not the database layer.
- Keep Mongo and in-memory demos thin and removable. Do not “upgrade” them unless asked.
- Python packaging: **uv** (`pyproject.toml` + `uv.lock`). No `requirements.txt`.

## Primary path style

Thin routes → helpers → response models. Copy `app/routes/sql_items.py` + `app/db/items.py` + `app/web/`, not fat Mongo/in-memory handlers.

```python
# ✅ GOOD — route delegates
row = await items_repo.create_item(item.name, item.description)
return _parse_response(row)

# ❌ BAD — SQL / business logic stuffed in the route
await conn.execute("INSERT INTO ...")
```

## URLs and auth intent

- `/api` → JSON (machines); `/auth` → HTML session; `/ui` → pages + HTMX partials (no `/htmx` prefix).
- Browsers: session + CSRF. API: opaque Bearer tokens in SQLite (not JWT by default). `require_user` accepts session or Bearer; **session + mutating `/api` requires CSRF**; Bearer does not.
- Do not rename the `items` domain until `ENGINEERING.md` says so.

## When you change architecture

Update `docs/ENGINEERING.md` in the same change. Stay in scope; do not invent new patterns.
